  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-33" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:27.67pt"&gt;General&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Business Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Respondent is a limited liability company formed in 2015 under the laws of the state of Delaware. The Respondent is a wholly-owned subsidiary of UGI Energy Services (&#8220;UGIES&#8221;). UGIES is a second-tier subsidiary of UGI Corporation. The Respondent is engaged in providing transportation services of shipper supplied natural gas through the Mt Bethel pipeline, which commenced on July 1, 2016. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The services are performed under tariffs and rates subject to the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&#8220;FERC&#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Company Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Respondent has no employees and relies on the operation and administrative services provided by UGIES, as well as by third party contractors for the pipeline&#8217;s operations and maintenance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:27.67pt"&gt;Summary Of Significant Account Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:54pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;A.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:8.57pt"&gt;Basis Of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements included in this Form were prepared in accordance with the accounting and reporting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in its Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases prescribed for natural gas companies subject to the provisions of the Natural Gas Act. Therefore, financial statements can contain differences from financial statements prepared in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles, including account classification, presentation of income taxes, and capitalization or balance sheet classification of costs that would otherwise be expensed under generally accepted accounting principles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:54pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;B.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:8.57pt"&gt;Use Of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The preparation of financial statements, along with the accompanying notes, requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the amounts for assets, liabilities, revenues, and expenses. These estimates and assumptions are based on management&#8217;s knowledge of current events and / or historical experience that were believed to be reasonable at the time the financial statements were prepared. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:54pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;C.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:8.01pt"&gt;Property, Plant, &amp;amp; Equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Property, plant, and equipment is recorded at original costs. For assets the company constructs, direct costs, such as labor, materials, and contractors, and indirect costs, such as administrative and overheads, plus an Allowance For Funds Used During Construction (&#8220;AFUDC&#8221;), are capitalized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:54pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;D.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:8.01pt"&gt;Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;UGI Mt Bethel Pipeline Company, LLC has no employees. Pipeline operations and maintenance are performed by UGIES field employees. The Respondent is also billed administrative and corporate overhead costs from UGIES. The Respondent will reimburse UGIES for such activities using agreed upon cost allocation procedures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:54pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;E.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:8.57pt"&gt;Gas Imbalances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;In the course of providing transportation services to customers, the Respondent may receive quantities of gas from shippers that differ from the quantities of gas delivered on behalf of the shipper, resulting in gas transportation imbalances. These imbalances are settled according to the provisions of the approved tariff. During the period from the date of commencement of operations to March 31, 2025, the Respondent delivered to UGI Gas Utilities the quantity of gas received from Transco. UGI Utilities is currently the sole shipper requiring natural gas transportation services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:54pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;F.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.13pt"&gt;Pension &amp;amp; Post Retirement Benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Respondent has no employees. Field labor is provided by UGIES. Administrative and corporate support is provided by UGIES. Therefore, the Respondent does not have any pension, other post retirement benefit, or post employment benefit plans.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%;padding-left:27.67pt"&gt;Disclosures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:12pt;padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;a.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;There are no significant financial disclosures to report for UGI Mt Bethel Pipeline Company, LLC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;b.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;There are no contingent Assets or Liabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;c.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:10.23pt"&gt;UGI Mt. Bethel Pipeline Company, LLC has no employees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;d.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;The acquired assets mainly consisted of 12.5 miles of pipe, rights of way, and overhead costs, with no compression or metering stations. As such, asset retirement obligations are determined to be insignificant.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;e.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;No environmental credits were received during the reporting period.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;f.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:12.46pt"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;g.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;h.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;There are no retained earnings restrictions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;i.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:13.01pt"&gt;There were no significant financial changes directly affecting gas pipeline operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;j.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:13.01pt"&gt;There are no unsettled rate proceedings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;k.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:10.23pt"&gt;None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;l.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:13.01pt"&gt;There were no significant changes in accounting methods during the year, which had an impact on net income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;m.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:6.9pt"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;n.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:72pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;o.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;There are no notes reflected specifically for UGI Mt Bethel Pipeline Company, LLC in the UGI Corporation and Subsidiaries annual consolidated financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
